    },
    {
      "id": "burst-and-cleanup",
      "title": "Survive a burst",
      "interviewerPrompt": "The feed now sends 720 messages in about 1.2 seconds. Keep the book right, keep the screen near ten book updates a second, and leave nothing running after a switch or when the page closes.",
      "constraints": [
        "Let each message change your data as it arrives, and draw the book on a 100 ms timer instead of on every message.",
        "Use a timer, not `requestAnimationFrame`: animation frames may not run in the offscreen frame the checks use, and they fire up to 120 times a second, which is not a cadence of ten.",
        "Keep `ref={bookRef}` on `.book` with the rows inside it. `.update-meter` counts the book's DOM updates and reads `Within budget` up to 20 a second.",
        "Leave no timer or socket running after the page closes, and none from an old scenario after a switch."
      ],
      "frameworkTests": [
        {
