              "selector": ".ask .price",
              "index": 0,
              "text": "101.00",
              "match": "equals"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": ".ask .size",
              "index": 0,
              "text": "19",
              "match": "equals"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": ".bid .price",
              "index": 9,
              "text": "94.00",
              "match": "equals"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": ".ask .price",
              "index": 9,
              "text": "106.50",
              "match": "equals"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure-book-switch-and-close",
          "name": "Round 3 · Switching mid-stream starts clean, and no socket or timer outlives its scenario",
          "steps": [
            {
              "type": "waitForCount",
              "selector": ".bid",
              "count": 10,
              "timeoutMs": 2500
            },
            {
              "type": "wait",
              "durationMs": 800
            },
            {
              "type": "setValue",
              "selector": ".scenario",
              "value": "late-snapshot"
            },
            {
              "type": "waitForText",
              "selector": ".last-seq",
              "text": "Last update #1030",
              "match": "equals",
              "timeoutMs": 4000
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": ".resync-count",
              "text": "0 resyncs",
              "match": "equals"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": ".ask .price",
              "index": 0,
              "text": "101.00",
              "match": "equals"
            },
            {
              "type": "setValue",
              "selector": ".scenario",
              "value": "burst"
            },
            {
              "type": "wait",
              "durationMs": 700
            },
            {
              "type": "setValue",
              "selector": ".scenario",
              "value": "gap"
            },
            {
              "type": "wait",
              "durationMs": 300
            },
            {
              "type": "unmountPreview"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectNoPreviewTimers"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "debrief": {
    "title": "You kept the book right at socket speed",
    "summary": "You built an order book from a snapshot and a socket of deltas, made the sequence numbers decide what to keep, recovered from a lost message without blanking the screen, and kept a 720-message burst off the render path. The interview signal is separating the data, which must be exact, from the screen, which only has to be current.",
    "takeaways": [
      "A snapshot is a sequence number as much as a book: every queued message is compared with it.",
      "A gap is not an error to show; it is a reason to load the book again while the old one stays readable.",
      "Fast data and fast rendering are different problems: change the data at socket speed and draw on a fixed cadence.",
      "A timer sets the cadence; an animation frame only says when the browser is about to paint. In a real app the two combine: draw on the first frame after 100 ms have passed."
    ],
    "frameworkNotes": {
      "react": "One effect per scenario owns the connection, the queue and the draw timer, and its cleanup closes all of them. The full book lives in maps inside that effect; only the best levels per side are React state."
    }
  },
